WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Manage your sign-in methods. Open Sign-in and security. Connected providers are listed here; provider connections are disabled in this demo.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Enable MFA only after verification. Confirm your identity, add an authenticator and verify its code. Setup keys and recovery codes stay private.

3
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:19.000
Review sessions and security activity. Identify your current session and investigate unfamiliar activity. Session identifiers are hidden in this video.

4
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Organization policy has a different scope. MFA is optional by default. An Owner can require it for access to organization data.

5
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Enroll your own authenticator first. Review the requirement before enabling the organization policy. Members need MFA when the policy requires it.

6
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:38.000
Keep a working way to sign in. Set a password before disconnecting a provider. This walkthrough leaves authentication settings unchanged.
